<figure>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 312" role="img" aria-labelledby="tl-title">
    <title id="tl-title">Diagram: task run lifecycle — queued to running to succeeded, failed, or canceled; failed runs retry back to queued with exponential backoff, and a catch-up window replays schedule runs missed while asleep.</title>
    <defs>
      <marker id="tl-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arrowhead" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Side note -->
    <text class="label start" x="40" y="44">laptop was asleep?</text>
    <text class="label muted start" x="40" y="60">catch-up window replays missed schedule runs</text>

    <!-- States -->
    <rect class="box" x="40" y="120" width="130" height="48" rx="8" />
    <text x="105" y="149">queued</text>

    <line class="arrow" x1="170" y1="144" x2="239" y2="144" marker-end="url(#tl-arrow)" />

    <rect class="box" x="240" y="120" width="130" height="48" rx="8" />
    <text x="305" y="149">running</text>

    <line class="arrow" x1="370" y1="132" x2="478" y2="82" marker-end="url(#tl-arrow)" />
    <line class="arrow" x1="370" y1="144" x2="478" y2="154" marker-end="url(#tl-arrow)" />
    <line class="arrow" x1="370" y1="156" x2="478" y2="226" marker-end="url(#tl-arrow)" />

    <rect class="box accent" x="480" y="60" width="140" height="44" rx="8" />
    <text class="accent-text" x="550" y="87">succeeded</text>

    <rect class="box" x="480" y="132" width="140" height="44" rx="8" />
    <text x="550" y="159">failed</text>

    <rect class="box" x="480" y="204" width="140" height="44" rx="8" />
    <text x="550" y="231">canceled</text>

    <!-- Retry loop: failed back to queued -->
    <path class="arrow" d="M 620 154 H 650 V 290 H 105 V 169" marker-end="url(#tl-arrow)" />
    <text class="label muted" x="377" y="280">retries left? backoff 30s &#215; 2&#8319; (cap 10m)</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    At-least-once: a run can execute more than once, so tasks should be safe to repeat.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

